WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.313
Grocery and Vegetable Market.

2
00:00:02.593 --> 00:00:06.945
Day 35 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Everyday Life phase.

3
00:00:08.695 --> 00:00:09.719
The key idea.

4
00:00:09.999 --> 00:00:19.172
Today's goal: buy groceries at a supermarket, kirana store or vegetable market: quantities, prices, freshness, home delivery and bargaining.

5
00:00:20.522 --> 00:00:21.375
Part 1.

6
00:00:21.655 --> 00:00:22.615
Key words.

7
00:00:23.865 --> 00:00:25.209
Here is a quick table:

8
00:00:25.489 --> 00:00:49.169
Word or phrase, and Meaning. kilo (kg) / half a kilo or 250 grams: weights. a dozen (12) / half a dozen (6): eggs, bananas. a packet or a bottle or a bunch or a loaf: units (a bunch of coriander, a loaf of bread). fresh or ripe or raw or stale or rotten: condition of food. in stock or out of stock: available or not available.

9
00:00:49.449 --> 00:01:00.073
MRP or discount or offer or buy one get one: prices and deals. expiry date or best before: last safe date. aisle: a row in a supermarket.

10
00:01:01.423 --> 00:01:04.581
bill or receipt or carry bag: what you get at the end.

11
00:01:05.931 --> 00:01:06.805
Part 2.

12
00:01:07.085 --> 00:01:08.301
Questions you'll ask.

13
00:01:09.551 --> 00:01:10.597
Supermarket.

14
00:01:10.877 --> 00:01:14.887
Excuse me, where can I find the rice or cooking oil or detergent?

15
00:01:15.167 --> 00:01:16.554
Do you have brown bread?

16
00:01:16.834 --> 00:01:18.391
When will it be back in stock?

17
00:01:18.671 --> 00:01:21.722
Is this on offer? / Is there any discount on this?

18
00:01:22.002 --> 00:01:23.879
What's the expiry date on this milk?

19
00:01:24.159 --> 00:01:25.503
Can I get a carry bag?

20
00:01:25.783 --> 00:01:26.914
How much is it?

21
00:01:27.194 --> 00:01:28.623
Do you do home delivery?

22
00:01:28.903 --> 00:01:30.375
Is there a minimum order?

23
00:01:31.725 --> 00:01:33.645
Vegetable market or kirana.

24
00:01:33.925 --> 00:01:37.723
How much are the tomatoes? / How much for a kilo of onions?

25
00:01:38.003 --> 00:01:39.027
Are these fresh?

26
00:01:39.307 --> 00:01:40.544
When did they come in?

27
00:01:40.824 --> 00:01:42.275
Can I choose them myself?

28
00:01:42.555 --> 00:01:46.608
Give me half a kilo, please. / A quarter kilo of green chillies.

29
00:01:46.888 --> 00:01:49.832
Can you do 40 rupees? / What's your best price?

30
00:01:50.112 --> 00:01:51.925
Can you add some coriander, please?

31
00:01:52.205 --> 00:01:53.208
(often free).

32
00:01:53.488 --> 00:01:55.024
Can I pay by UPI?

33
00:01:56.374 --> 00:01:57.270
Part 3.

34
00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:00.217
Conversation 1: at the vegetable market.

35
00:02:01.467 --> 00:02:03.493
Here is how the conversation goes.

36
00:02:03.773 --> 00:02:05.907
Bhaiya, how much are the tomatoes?

37
00:02:06.187 --> 00:02:07.744
40 rupeesa kilo.

38
00:02:08.024 --> 00:02:09.283
And the onions?

39
00:02:09.563 --> 00:02:12.720
35. rupeesVery good quality, fresh this morning.

40
00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:13.939
Okay.

41
00:02:14.219 --> 00:02:17.675
One kilo of tomatoes and two kilos of onions.

42
00:02:17.955 --> 00:02:20.387
Can I choose the tomatoes myself?

43
00:02:21.737 --> 00:02:23.337
The conversation continues.

44
00:02:23.617 --> 00:02:25.302
Sure, take this basket.

45
00:02:25.582 --> 00:02:26.393
Thanks.

46
00:02:26.673 --> 00:02:28.529
And half a kilo of beans.

47
00:02:28.809 --> 00:02:30.067
Are these fresh?

48
00:02:30.347 --> 00:02:31.649
Yes, very fresh.

49
00:02:31.929 --> 00:02:34.126
That's 150 rupeestotal.

50
00:02:34.406 --> 00:02:36.838
Can you do 140 rupees?

51
00:02:37.118 --> 00:02:39.273
And add some coriander, please.

52
00:02:39.553 --> 00:02:42.923
Okay, 140. rupeesHere's the coriander.

53
00:02:44.273 --> 00:02:45.873
The conversation continues.

54
00:02:46.153 --> 00:02:47.071
Thank you!

55
00:02:47.351 --> 00:02:49.079
I'll pay by UPI.

56
00:02:50.429 --> 00:02:51.346
Part 4.

57
00:02:51.626 --> 00:02:54.911
Conversation 2: supermarket, out of stock and billing.

58
00:02:56.161 --> 00:02:58.188
Here is how the conversation goes.

59
00:02:58.468 --> 00:03:01.071
Excuse me, where can I find the oats?

60
00:03:01.351 --> 00:03:03.676
Aisle 6, next to the breakfast cereals.

61
00:03:03.956 --> 00:03:06.815
I checked, but the 1-kilo pack is out of stock.

62
00:03:07.095 --> 00:03:08.631
Do you have any in the back?

63
00:03:08.911 --> 00:03:10.020
Let me check...

64
00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:11.985
Sorry, it'll come tomorrow.

65
00:03:12.265 --> 00:03:14.313
We have the 500-gram packs.

66
00:03:15.663 --> 00:03:17.263
The conversation continues.

67
00:03:17.543 --> 00:03:19.591
Okay, I'll take two of those.

68
00:03:19.871 --> 00:03:21.685
Is there an offer on them?

69
00:03:21.965 --> 00:03:23.821
Yes, 10% off on two.

70
00:03:24.101 --> 00:03:25.381
At the billing counter

71
00:03:25.661 --> 00:03:27.282
Do you have a membership card?

72
00:03:27.562 --> 00:03:28.693
No, I don't.

73
00:03:28.973 --> 00:03:30.807
Do I need one for the discount?

74
00:03:32.157 --> 00:03:33.757
The conversation continues.

75
00:03:34.037 --> 00:03:36.021
No, the discount is for everyone.

76
00:03:36.301 --> 00:03:37.731
Do you need a carry bag?

77
00:03:38.011 --> 00:03:39.099
No, thanks.

78
00:03:39.379 --> 00:03:40.765
I've brought my own.

79
00:03:41.045 --> 00:03:44.032
Your total is 1,240 rupees.

80
00:03:44.312 --> 00:03:45.677
Here's my card.

81
00:03:45.957 --> 00:03:48.240
Could I also get the bill on WhatsApp?

82
00:03:49.590 --> 00:03:50.550
Part 5.

83
00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:52.003
When things go wrong.

84
00:03:53.253 --> 00:03:54.661
This milk has expired.

85
00:03:54.941 --> 00:03:56.413
The date was yesterday.

86
00:03:56.693 --> 00:03:58.848
I think you've charged me twice for the rice.

87
00:03:59.128 --> 00:04:04.184
The price on the shelf is 99, rupeesbut the bill says 120 rupees.

88
00:04:04.464 --> 00:04:05.893
Some of the eggs are broken.

89
00:04:06.173 --> 00:04:07.496
Could I exchange them?

90
00:04:07.776 --> 00:04:10.101
My online order is missing two items.

91
00:04:11.451 --> 00:04:12.390
Part 6.

92
00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:13.587
Practice.

93
00:04:14.837 --> 00:04:22.603
Write a shopping list with quantities in English (8 items), for example, 1 kg rice, a dozen eggs, a bunch of spinach.

94
00:04:22.883 --> 00:04:23.608
Fix:

95
00:04:23.888 --> 00:04:27.280
Give one kg onion. / What is rate of tomato?

96
00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:29.547
Success:

97
00:04:29.827 --> 00:04:30.681
Answers.

98
00:04:30.961 --> 00:04:35.142
Could I have a kilo of onions, please? / How much are the tomatoes?

99
00:04:36.492 --> 00:04:37.431
Part 7.

100
00:04:37.711 --> 00:04:38.756
Speak today.

101
00:04:40.006 --> 00:04:44.465
Buy something using English quantities: half a kilo, a dozen, a packet of...

102
00:04:44.745 --> 00:04:47.198
Ask one question about price or freshness.

103
00:04:48.548 --> 00:04:50.084
That's the end of this lesson.

104
00:04:50.364 --> 00:04:55.015
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

105
00:04:55.295 --> 00:05:01.417
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

